{ A declaration past the 4096 characters `DiagLine` holds, which is the one
  shape that reaches the outline's documented fallback: the server slices the
  spelling the programmer wrote out of the line it holds, and here it has no
  such column -- so the folded name the compiler reported is the answer, and
  the reader sees `latername` where the source says `LaterName`.

  It exists because both readers of a `symbol` line take the name from a
  field, and one of them was reading the wrong field: ADR-0253 widened the
  line and the name moved from 7 to 9. Every other session here reads a
  source it can slice, so the wrong field was overwritten before anyone saw
  it, and the suite was green over an outline that would have printed a
  column of end-line numbers. }
program wideline;
var Early: integer;
{  } var LaterName: integer;
begin
  Early := 1;
  LaterName := Early
end.
